{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"110019","commit":"877b73f433cdd76b55bc4e46fa17bce8c9db9140","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The method `result()` in `PlainActionFuture` and `PlainActionFuture.Sync` now throws `ExecutionException`. This change is consistent across the codebase, but it\u0027s important to ensure that all call sites handle this exception properly. The addition of `assertDoesNotThrow` in several test cases helps with this, but developers should be aware of the potential for `ExecutionException` when calling `result()`.\nThe removal of the special handling for `RuntimeException` in `PlainActionFuture.Sync.getValue()` simplifies the code and aligns it with the updated method signature. However, this change might affect behavior if there were specific expectations around how `RuntimeException` was handled before.\nThe introduction of `ThrowingSupplier` in both `ProgressListenableActionFuture` and `ESTestCase` is a useful utility that reduces boilerplate code when dealing with methods that can throw exceptions. This should improve maintainability and readability.\nThe changes to test cases, such as using `assertDoesNotThrow` and updating exception assertions, ensure that the tests are robust and cover the new behavior introduced by these changes. This is crucial for maintaining the reliability of the codebase.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/action/support/PlainActionFutureTests.java-server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/action/support/PlainActionFutureTests.java-6238:6279,6403:6444-","promptId":"#FNCXY","srcPath":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/action/support/PlainActionFutureTests.java","dstPath":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/action/support/PlainActionFutureTests.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":6238,"endPos":6279,"startLine":129,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":129,"endLineOffset":49,"length":42},{"pos":6403,"endPos":6444,"startLine":134,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":134,"endLineOffset":53,"len