rarchy as it\u0027s used to prevent excessive nesting of execution exceptions here, but this one is private."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/blob-cache/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/blobcache/common/ProgressListenableActionFuture.java","id":37391,"created_at":"2024-06-21T01:51:07Z","original_position":29,"side":"RIGHT","position":34,"submitted_on_commit":"877b73f433cdd76b55bc4e46fa17bce8c9db9140","diff_hunk":"@@ -200,14 +200,34 @@ public void addListener(ActionListener\u003cLong\u003e listener, long value) {\n         assert invariant();\n     }\n \n-    private static void executeListener(final ActionListener\u003cLong\u003e listener, final Supplier\u003cLong\u003e result) {\n+    /**\n+     * Return the result of this future, if it has been completed successfully, or unwrap and throw the exception with which it was\n+     * completed exceptionally. It is not valid to call this method if the future is incomplete.\n+     */\n+    private Long actionResult() throws Exception {\n+        try {\n+            return result();\n+        } catch (ExecutionException e) {\n+            if (e.getCause() instanceof Exception exCause) {\n+                throw exCause;\n+            } else {\n+                throw e;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }","submitted_line":217},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]},{"groundTruth":{"original_line":333,"line":333,"comment_lines":["[][333]"],"review_comment":["align with `@param` name"],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/action/support/PlainActionFuture.java","id":37389,"created_at":"2024-06-21T01:36:21Z","original_position":79,"side":"RIGHT","position":79,"submitted_on_commit":"877b73f433cdd76b55bc4e46fa17bce8c9db9140","diff_hunk":"@@ -358,7 +330,7 @@ boolean cancel() {\n         }\n \n         /**\n-         * Implementation of completing a task.  Either {@code v} or {@code t} will\n+         * Implementation of completing a task.  Either {@code v} or {@code e} will","submitted_line":333},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]},{"groundTruth":{"original_line":182,"line":182,"comment_lines":["[][182]"],"review_comment":["This is not quite the same as before, I believe previously, if there was a `RuntimeException` it would be thrown directly, and if there was a checked exception the behaviour would be consistent with the above. But looking up the call stack there doesn\u0027t appear to be any behaviour specific to the exception thrown. I\u0027m happy to try and restore the original behaviour but fear it might just be adding noise to be consistent with something that nobody was depending on in the first place.","Yes I think this is ok, indeed possibly preferable, because now we get the call stack to the `.result()` call as well as the one which failed the future."],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/indices/TimestampFieldMapperService.java","id":37390,"created_at":"2024-06-21T01:43:07Z","original_position":27,"side":"RIGHT","position":27,"submitted_on_commit":"877b73f433cdd76b55bc4e46fa17bce8c9db9140","diff_hunk":"@@ -172,8 +174,12 @@ public DateFieldMapper.DateFieldType getTimestampFieldType(Index index) {\n         if (future \u003d\u003d null || future.isDone() \u003d\u003d false) {\n             return null;\n         }\n-        // call non-blocking actionResult() as we could be on a network or scheduler thread which we must not block\n-        return future.actionResult();\n+        // call non-blocking result() as we could be on a network or scheduler thread which we must not block\n+        try {\n+            return future.result();\n+        } catch (ExecutionException e) {\n+            throw new UncategorizedExecutionException(\"An error occurred fetching timestamp field type for \" + index, e);\n+        }","submitted_line":182},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The method `result()` in `PlainActionFuture` and `PlainActionFuture.Sync` now throws `ExecutionException`. This change is consistent across the codebase, but it\u0027s important to ensure that all call sites handle this exception properly. The addition of `assertDoesNotThrow` in several test cases helps with this, but developers should be aware of the potential for `ExecutionException` when calling `result()`.\nThe removal of the special handling for `RuntimeException` in `PlainActionFuture.Sync.getValue()` simplifies the code and aligns it with the updated method signature. However, this change might affect behavior if there were specific expectations around how `RuntimeException` was handled before.\nThe introduction of `ThrowingSupplier` in both `ProgressListenableActionFuture` and `ESTestCase` is a useful utility that reduces boilerplate code when dealing with methods that can throw exceptions. This should improve maintainability and readability.\nThe changes to test cases, such as using `assertDoesNotThrow` and updating exception assertions, ensure that the tests are robust and cover the new behavior introduced by these changes. This is crucial for maintaining the reliability of the codebase.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/action/support/PlainActionFutureTests.java-server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/action/support/PlainActionFutureTests.java-6238:6279,6403:6444-","promptId":"#FNCXY","srcPath":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/action/support/PlainActionFutureTests.java","dstPath":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/action/support/PlainActionFutureTests.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":6238,"endPos":6279,"startLine":129,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":129,"endLineOffset":49,"length":42},{"pos":6403,"endPos":6444,"startLine":134,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":134,"endLineOffset":53,"length":42}],"dstChanges":[]},{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/action/support/PlainActionFuture.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/action/support/PlainActionFuture.java-6455:6463,6463:6486,6533:6557,6557:6586,6679:6703,6703:6727,6735:6738,6738:6777,6777:6796,7050:7066,7066:7158-6774:6792,6792:6836,6911:6970,7001:7007,7008:7026","promptId":"#0VSHX","